# Orchestration artifacts

Full contracts: [`.cursor/agents/orchestrator.md`](.cursor/agents/orchestrator.md), [`.cursor/agents/planner.md`](.cursor/agents/planner.md), [`.cursor/agents/builder.md`](.cursor/agents/builder.md), [`.cursor/agents/test.md`](.cursor/agents/test.md), [`.cursor/agents/validator.md`](.cursor/agents/validator.md).

**Templates** ([`.cursor/orchestrations/_template/`](.cursor/orchestrations/_template/)): `task-manifest.json`, `plan.md`, `acceptance-criteria.md`, `build-log.md`, `test-report.md`, `validation-report.md`, `human-approval.md`, and [`README.md`](.cursor/orchestrations/_template/README.md) (copy into `{task-id}/` when bootstrapping). Cross-cutting audit items: [`docs/validation-checklist.md`](../docs/validation-checklist.md).

## Path

Runs live under **`.cursor/orchestrations/{task-id}/`**. Do not treat orchestration files as application source — they record pipeline state and stage outputs.

## `task-manifest.json` — Orchestrator only

- **Only the Orchestrator** (or a human following the same contract) may create or update **`task-manifest.json`**.
- **Planner, Builder, Test, and Validator** must **not** edit the manifest — read-only for `task_id`, `objective`, `locked_artifacts`, `loop_count`, etc.
- Manifest fields such as `risk_tier`, `gate_status`, `completed_stages`, `rework_count`, `rework_history`, `session_counts`, `command_evidence`, `flags`, and `human_approval` are Orchestrator-owned routing and audit state. Other agents report facts in their owned artifact; the Orchestrator mirrors summaries into the manifest when routing.

## Per-stage writes (under `{task-id}/`)

| Agent | May write |
|-------|-----------|
| **Orchestrator** | `task-manifest.json`; `human-approval.md` when recording Gate 6 approval, rejection, or rework |
| **Planner** | `plan.md`, `acceptance-criteria.md` |
| **Builder** | `build-log.md` only (plus application code per plan). **Not** `plan.md`, manifest, or other orchestration files |
| **Test** | `test-report.md` only |
| **Validator** | `validation-report.md` only |

## Locks and scope

- **`locked_artifacts`:** treat listed paths as read-only unless the manifest is updated to unlock (Orchestrator/human).
- **Do not** expand scope via orchestration edits — `plan.md` is design truth; deviations belong in **`build-log.md`** under **Deviations from plan**.

## Pipeline

Default order: **Orchestrator → Planner → Builder → Test → Validator → Orchestrator** (human approval / loops per Orchestrator rules). After editing artifacts, align with the manifest’s **`current_agent`** and completed-stage contracts before invoking the next agent. Validator **FAIL** and human `rejected_rework` outcomes return to Builder, then continue through Test and Validator unless the Orchestrator routes back to Planner for a scope-changing rework.
